CSV guide, Parquet guide, JSON guide

CREATE TABLE csv_snapshot AS SELECT * FROM 'data.csv'; -- Store a copy
SHOW TABLES;
DESCRIBE csv_snapshot;
SELECT * FROM csv_snapshot LIMIT 10;

CREATE VIEW source_data AS SELECT * FROM 'data.csv'; -- Save a query
SELECT * FROM source_data LIMIT 10;

A table stores a snapshot; changes to the source file do not update it. A view stores the query and reads the source when queried, so the file must remain accessible. Create each table or view once, then query it in later sessions. Use a database file to keep these objects after exiting. Tables, Views

